#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373028 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c07721dd-4b97-5d57-8de1-5098117e3071" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04a5b74a-50ea-55b7-be9a-d53bc73a1686" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373030} {:answer/id #uuid "00287bb1-7e3c-56c5-bd02-121fa67b877f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 8 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373031} {:answer/id #uuid "de09d4be-8d92-5f4a-bd88-ac539e2ca901" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373032} {:answer/id #uuid "1f6fb764-6b5b-5040-9f8c-50374c9e41e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373033} {:answer/id #uuid "ef19a6d6-4434-52fb-ab98-6ceab6ab9c86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de09d4be-8d92-5f4a-bd88-ac539e2ca901" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373032} :answer-field/id #uuid "50551604-a11e-5a98-ab1c-a6bbadaa2c7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373029}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6d9b6de3-4396-5c82-b41c-2429c7a1964b" :question/math-academy-id "q-140472" :question/problem "Find the orthogonal projection of the vector $x$ onto the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $v$ and $w$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSince our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{v,w}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ v & w \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}6 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 5\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373035 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad9f55b2-ce37-507f-8cb6-7d4e30e6868a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25f30edb-65c6-57e5-a87a-2942c767fb84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373037} {:answer/id #uuid "da1e2779-04b4-5668-96b5-e5dc7e6153d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373038} {:answer/id #uuid "6b604f6b-e3cd-5806-9ab8-b1eebbe5ca81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373039} {:answer/id #uuid "81378202-50c6-5cfb-9d56-d87add70a867" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373040} {:answer/id #uuid "7b1ad9e8-429b-5525-a1ec-ac537d61988f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81378202-50c6-5cfb-9d56-d87add70a867" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373040} :answer-field/id #uuid "5993fcab-56d3-5a1e-b900-f1a9dff0b051" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373036}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8b3010e0-dd5b-598a-b59c-b5757e33b454" :question/math-academy-id "q-140473" :question/problem "Find the vector in the subspace spanned by ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ \nthat is closest to the vector $x,$ where \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe closest vector to $x$ in the subspace spanned by ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace, which is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{30}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373042 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad9f55b2-ce37-507f-8cb6-7d4e30e6868a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8921d29e-90ca-5250-bc27-9d64ca5ad81f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373044} {:answer/id #uuid "241d34f7-6b6f-5de6-a8d6-12a65a3952de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373045} {:answer/id #uuid "37affad6-37a4-5a6b-a726-61e360cc673b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373046} {:answer/id #uuid "2ce07f33-331e-5dd2-9a85-98167f4eafc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373047} {:answer/id #uuid "d22983a7-51c0-56b0-910c-ebbc06c54fda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373048}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "241d34f7-6b6f-5de6-a8d6-12a65a3952de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373045} :answer-field/id #uuid "7724db94-374e-5532-a1f6-00d291074518" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373043}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c94191a-43a1-5922-ab22-a6d441b65abc" :question/math-academy-id "q-140474" :question/problem "Verify whether the vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ are linearly independent, and find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we verify whether ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ are linearly independent. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -9\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -7\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+7{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, the pivot columns correspond to the linearly independent vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ that form the basis of our span.\n\nNow, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the linearly independent columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 11\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{54}[\\begin{aligned}11 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373049 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad9f55b2-ce37-507f-8cb6-7d4e30e6868a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07e67ba4-c5bc-51b4-8b94-48e0b9249764" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373051} {:answer/id #uuid "cee3e6a6-60eb-5430-bda7-2d611d94d445" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373052} {:answer/id #uuid "0ea41735-e9e3-5b22-ac5a-ccde88cde448" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373053} {:answer/id #uuid "cf4cb458-878d-55ac-80cb-d1daa8c12f7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373054} {:answer/id #uuid "1cd01e94-d2e8-5f5a-9530-ca5ddb6c3ffe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07e67ba4-c5bc-51b4-8b94-48e0b9249764" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373051} :answer-field/id #uuid "71f9b5d5-cf31-5ef9-97f9-972e1c9edf6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373050}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c81253d2-77a0-5506-9613-10f000472aac" :question/math-academy-id "q-158124" :question/problem "Find the vector in the subspace spanned by ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ \nthat is closest to the vector $x,$ where \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe closest vector to $x$ in the subspace spanned by ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace, which is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}34 & -8 \\\\ -8 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{38}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 34\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373056 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c07721dd-4b97-5d57-8de1-5098117e3071" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c515b014-53d0-58ee-ad42-badc30243574" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :a