^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSince our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{v,w}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ v & w \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 14\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
